e you priority but fewer caballeros. Low cards flood your court with troops but leave you picking last.\n\nPlay your 13 and you choose first from the action cards - but you recruit zero caballeros. Play your 1 and you’ll get six fresh troops - but you’re choosing from whatever scraps remain.\n\nThis creates an agonising push-pull that never gets old. Every single card play is a sacrifice. Do you burn the 13 now to grab that devastating action card, or save it for the final scoring round when positioning matters most? Do you go low to stockpile forces, gambling that no one takes the card you need?\n\nNine decisions. Thirteen cards. And every single one of them matters.\n\n## Action Cards: Controlled Chaos#\n\nEach round, five action cards are revealed - one from each stack. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEl Grande | Board Game | BoardGameGeek (https://boardgamegeek.com/boardgame/93/el-grande/files)\nciteturn2search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; N/A Wolfgang Kramer, Richard Ulrich + 0 more ... El Grande - Cartas de Acción en castellano en formato Euro (59x92mm). ... Cartas en castellano, listas para imprimir, FAQ incluidos.\n\n# El Grande (1995)\n\nUse your caballeros to control regions of medieval Spain, keeping clear of the King!\n\n  * 34K Ratings & 6.7K Comments · GeekBuddy Analysis\n\n## Game Information\n\n  * ### Number of Players\n\n2–5 Players\n\nCommunity: (no votes) 3–5 — Best: 5\n\n  * ### Play Time\n\n60–120 Min\n\nPlaying Time\n\n  * ### Suggested Age\n\nAge: 12+\n\nCommunity: 12+\n\n  * ### Complexity\n\nWeight: –– 2.93 / 5 Complexity Rating\n\n'Complexity' Rating Results Learn more about complexity ratings\n\n### Game Credits\n\n  * #### Alternate Names\n\nエルグランデ + 3 more\n  * #### Designer\n\nN/A Wolfgang Kramer, Richard Ulrich + 0 more\n  * #### Artist\n\nN/A Doris Matthäus, Stefan Sonnberger, Franz-Georg Stämmele + 0 more\n  * #### Publisher\n\nN/A Hans im Glück + 15 more\n\n### New rules o